@startuml
title Local-First Synchronisation Order (~--local-first)

start
:Validate authentication, service reachability\nand system time safety gates;
note right
  Operating context:
  ~--sync ~--local-first or ~--monitor ~--local-first.

  ~--local-first changes reconciliation order.
  It does NOT mean that a local file may blindly
  overwrite an independently changed online file.
end note

:Process known database state against\nthe local filesystem first;
note right
  Detect and action locally modified or deleted
  objects that were previously tracked.
end note

:Scan local filesystem for new data;
:Upload eligible new local files / directories;
note right
  Modified tracked files still fetch current online
  metadata before replacement. If a genuine or
  unresolved online conflict exists, local data is
  preserved before conflict resolution continues.
end note

:Reconcile Microsoft OneDrive online state;
note right
  Remote reconciliation still applies after
  the local pass. ~--local-first changes ordering;
  it does not disable conflict protection.
end note

:Apply remaining online changes locally;
stop
@enduml
